  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{\u2032}(t)=\u27e8-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}\u27e9\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=\u27e82,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)\u27e9.$\n\n$F(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e8-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}\u27e9\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e8-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}\u27e9\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=\u27e82,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)\u27e9$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=\u27e8\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e82,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e88+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e82,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2)\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-6$ and ${c}_{2}=0.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e8\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t+1)\u27e9.\n$$",
